1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,678
HailBytes SAT runs from a paid AWS Marketplace AMI. Before Terraform can launch it, the account has to be subscribed, and a few account-level things checked. This chapter does both, once.

2
00:00:14,678 --> 00:00:34,303
Subscribing is a console action. Open the listing signed in to the deploying account, choose Continue to Subscribe, then Accept Terms, and wait for the confirmation. There is no command-line equivalent, and Terraform cannot do it for you.

3
00:00:34,303 --> 00:00:52,025
If you skip it, nothing complains at plan time. The apply builds the network and the database, then the first instance launch fails with OptInRequired. And seeing the AMI proves nothing: Marketplace AMIs are visible to every account.

4
00:00:52,025 --> 00:01:08,442
Open CloudShell in the region you will deploy to. The S3 state locking we use in chapter two needs Terraform 1.10 or newer; if CloudShell has none, install it into your home directory, which persists.

5
00:01:08,442 --> 00:01:18,773
First, the service-linked roles that the database, cache and load balancer services need. Creating one is account-wide, one-time, and costs nothing.

6
00:01:21,468 --> 00:01:32,233
Here the preflight confirms the AMI is published in this region, and says plainly that this is not proof of a subscription.

7
00:01:35,103 --> 00:01:51,086
Then quota. The HA tier uses two Elastic IPs, one NAT gateway per zone, and the default limit is five per region. So a third client in the same region needs an increase first.

8
00:01:51,086 --> 00:02:00,981
Read the output, not just the exit code. A NOT ENOUGH here still ends normally, and fails the apply later.

9
00:02:02,481 --> 00:02:19,768
One more thing the preflight prints: the deploying identity needs some IAM permissions, because every tier creates its own least-privilege role for the instances. A role that can only create EC2 and RDS resources fails partway through.

10
00:02:19,768 --> 00:02:27,490
The account is ready. In chapter two we deploy HailBytes SAT with the quickstart root.
